models/*.obj filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
models/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Shell scripts must stay LF-only regardless of a contributor's global
# core.autocrlf - a CRLF shebang/body breaks bash execution outright on
# macOS/Linux (this bit the new scripts/build_and_deploy_macos.sh: Windows
# git was about to silently convert it to CRLF on the next checkout).
*.sh text eol=lf

# NanoVDB grid files (pbrt_scenes/nanovdb-*.nvdb) are raw binary blobs with
# no attribute of their own here - without `-text`, a Windows checkout with
# the (default) core.autocrlf=true would silently LF->CRLF-convert any
# embedded 0x0A byte that isn't a real line ending, corrupting the file.
# This is the same class of bug the *.sh rule above already fixes, just
# for a binary asset instead of a script.
#
# NOTE: this was ORIGINALLY (and incorrectly) believed to be the cause of
# tests/unit/pbrt_cpu_builder_tests.cpp's NanoVdbTemperatureNameProduces
# RealEmission failing on the Windows CI runner ("corrupt file, wrong
# gridname, or an unsupported NanoVDB grid type") - that diagnosis was
# WRONG (the failure persisted on the very next CI run after this rule
# landed); the real cause was a working-directory/relative-path bug in
# .github/workflows/unit-tests.yml, fixed separately. This rule is kept
# anyway as still-correct, harmless practice for a binary asset - just
# don't assume it explains that specific test failure.
*.nvdb -text
